## §B. Network Topology and Graph-Theoretic Foundations

**Definition B.1 (Communication Graph).** At time $t$, the AIADN topology is $G(t) = (\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{E}(t))$, where $(a_i, a_j) \in \mathcal{E}(t)$ iff agent $i$ can transmit to $j$ at time $t$.

**Definition B.2 (Orchestration Hierarchy).** AIADN maintains a three-level hierarchy: Level 0 (Cognitive Core orchestrator $\mathcal{O}$), Level 1 (elected type coordinators $\ell_\tau(t)$), Level 2 (peer agents). This structure is unchanged from v1 but is now formally coupled to the Digital Twin layer (§I).

**Definition B.3 (Graph Laplacian).** For weighted adjacency matrix $W(t)$:

$$L(t) = D(t) - W(t) \tag{B.1}$$

**Lemma B.1 (Connectivity under Random Link Failures).** Under Assumption A.2, expected algebraic connectivity satisfies:

$$\mathbb{E}[\lambda_2(L(t))] \geq p_{\min} \cdot \lambda_2(L^{\text{nom}}) > 0 \tag{B.2}$$

**Proof.** Each edge is independently active with probability $\geq p_{\min}$, so $\mathbb{E}[W(t)] \geq p_{\min} W^{\text{nom}}$ component-wise. Monotonicity of algebraic connectivity in the Laplacian (Cheeger inequality) gives (B.2). $\square$

**Extension B.1 (DoS Attack Resilience).** Under intermittent Denial-of-Service attacks modeled as Bernoulli packet erasures with adversarial rate $\rho_a \in [0,1)$, the effective link probability becomes $p_{ij}^{\text{eff}} = p_{ij}(1 - \rho_a)$. Lemma B.1 continues to hold with $p_{\min}$ replaced by $p_{\min}(1 - \rho_a)$, provided $\rho_a < 1 - \lambda_2^{\min}/(p_{\min} \lambda_2(L^{\text{nom}}))$, which defines a **maximum tolerable attack rate** beyond which connectivity guarantees are lost. This bound is evaluated for MSAT parameters in §J.

