## §D. Task Completion Probability and Submodularity

**Definition D.1 (Task Completion Probability).** For task $j_k$ assigned to subset $\mathcal{A}_k$:

$$f_k(\mathcal{A}_k) = 1 - \prod_{i \in \mathcal{A}_k} \bigl(1 - g(\mathbf{c}_i, \mathbf{r}_k)\bigr), \quad g(\mathbf{c}_i, \mathbf{r}_k) = \min\!\left(1, \prod_{d=1}^D \frac{c_{id}}{r_{kd}}\right) \tag{D.1}$$

**Lemma D.1 (Submodularity of $f_k$).** *$f_k$ is normalized, monotone, and submodular.*

**Proof.** For $S \subseteq T \subseteq \mathcal{A}$, $a \notin T$, define $\phi_S = \prod_{i \in S}(1-g_i)$. Then $f_k(S \cup \{a\}) - f_k(S) = \phi_S \cdot g_a$ and $f_k(T \cup \{a\}) - f_k(T) = \phi_T \cdot g_a$. Since $S \subseteq T$ implies $\phi_S \geq \phi_T$, we have $\phi_S g_a \geq \phi_T g_a$, establishing the diminishing returns property. $\square$

